# Toss-Style Design System

## Design Direction

- Quiet, high-trust product UI: clear hierarchy, generous spacing, minimal ornament.
- One primary accent color; grayscale for most structure.
- No decorative gradients, heavy shadows, or competing accent colors.

## Typography

- Strict type scale: page title, section title, body, supporting text, metadata.
- Prefer font weight and color over large size jumps.
- Never pure black text — use dark grayscale foreground.
- Metrics: number dominant, unit smaller but legible.

## Layout and Rhythm

- Consistent spacing tokens; related content close, unrelated separated.
- Section rhythm: summary → details → action → context.
- No nested cards or excessive borders.

## Cards and Surfaces

- Cards only for grouped content that needs a surface.
- Restrained radius; subtle shadow OR border, not both heavily.
- Low shadow opacity; no important controls on low-contrast surfaces.

## Color

- Accent for primary actions, selected state, links.
- Semantic colors for status only (success, warning, error, info).
- Disabled/secondary in grayscale; never status by color alone.

## Dark Mode

- Rebuild grayscale scale for dark mode; don't invert.
- Reduce accent intensity on dark backgrounds.
- Test charts, cards, forms in both modes.

## Accessibility

- WCAG AA contrast; visible focus states; large tap targets.
- Semantic HTML and labels before ARIA; respect reduced motion.

## Common Mistakes

- One-off spacing values; multiple accent colors; card overuse; hero typography in dense screens.
